   "content": "<p>11. The marginal propensity to consume is</p><p>(a) ΔC/ΔT  (b) DS/DY  (c) C/Y  (d) S/Y</p><p>12. The marginal propensity to save is</p><p>(a) C/Y  (b) S/Y  (c) ΔS/ΔY  (d) Y/S</p><p>13. The income obtained from within the geographical boundaries of a country is called</p><p>(a) gross domestic product  (b) gross national product  (c) national income  (d) per capita income</p><p>14. The formula of per capita income is</p><p>(a) population ÷ national income  (b) national income ÷ population  (c) none</p><p>15. Zakat, gifts, unemployment allowance, pension and stipends are included in</p><p>(a) production cost  (b) gross domestic product  (c) transfer payments  (d) net national product</p><p>16. The marginal propensity to consume is</p><p>(a) I − MPS  (b) I + MPS  (c) S/Y  (d) none</p><p>17. The marginal propensity to save is</p><p>(a) I − MPC  (b) I + MPC  (c) C/Y  (d) S/Y</p><p>18. The average propensity to consume is</p><p>(a) S/Y  (b) I − APS  (c) DS/DY  (d) none</p><p>19. The average propensity to save is</p><p>(a) I − APC  (b) C/Y  (c) DS/DY  (d) I + MPS</p><p>20. What is not included in gross national product?</p><p>(a) services of housewives  (b) doctor’s fee  (c) services of the washerman  (d) income of the labourer</p>",
