     "text": "Professor Crowther objects to this theory that the quantity theory of money only tells how rises and falls occur in economic struggle and prices, but it has not told why after all these rises and falls occur. Then it also does not explain that whenever there is an increase in the quantity of money, an increase occurs in prices; but sometimes, when the demand for things in the market is low and purchasing becomes slack, then even by increasing the quantity of money prices cannot be raised. This is exactly like “a horse can be pulled by the reins up to the water, but if it is not thirsty, it cannot be compelled to drink water.”",
