   "content": "<p>Model paper questions</p><p>Short questions</p><p>Write the answers to the short questions.</p><p>1. What is meant by the barter system?</p><p>A. Such an economic system in which money does not exist, but the exchange of goods with goods, of goods with services, or of services with services is direct. It is also called the system of direct exchange.</p><p>2. State the definition of money.</p><p>A. Money is that thing which has obtained general acceptability as a medium of exchange and which at the same time also performs the duty of measure of value and store of value. Or: every thing which performs the functions of money is called money.</p><p>3. State four important functions of money.</p><p>A. (i) medium of exchange; (ii) measure of value; (iii) store of value; (iv) transfer of value.</p><p>4. Write four qualities of good money.</p><p>A. (i) general acceptability; (ii) durability; (iii) recognisability; (iv) divisibility.</p><p>5. What is meant by near money?</p><p>A. By it is meant that form of money which is not in liquid or cash (Cash) form and cannot be brought into use immediately in connection with buying and selling. However, it can be changed into cash money after a specified period, e.g. fixed deposits, government securities and shares of companies etc.</p><p>6. Write the definition of paper money.</p><p>A. By paper money are meant such notes as are issued by the government or by the central bank of the country. In Pakistan the notes of Rs 10, 20, 50 etc. are paper money.</p><p>7. What is convertible paper money called?</p><p>A. Such paper money as can be exchanged for gold or silver on the demand of the public is called convertible paper money. Behind these notes it keeps gold or silver in equal quantity.</p><p>8. What is meant by inconvertible paper money?</p><p>A. Such paper money as cannot be exchanged for gold or silver on the demand of the public is called inconvertible paper money. Behind these notes the government does not keep gold or silver in equal quantity.</p>",
