   "content": "<p>18. State four big heads of the expenses of the government.</p><p>A. They are as follows: (i) the government spends on construction work, e.g. roads etc.; (ii) the government spends to improve the system of education; (iii) the government spends on maintaining health, e.g. hospitals etc.; (iv) the government spends to improve the system of defence.</p><p>19. What is meant by private finance?</p><p>A. Common people too usually prepare their budget every month and make an estimate of income and expenditure; this is called private finance.</p><p>Section II (Section II)</p><p>Question 2. Write detailed answers to the following questions.</p><p>1. State the difference between private finance and public finance. (Sargodha Board 2009, Lahore Board 2010)</p><p>2. State the principles of imposing tax. (Multan Board 2009, Sargodha Board 2010)</p><p>3. Explain the different kinds of taxes. (Bahawalpur Board 2010)</p><p>4. Give the detail of the different sources of income of the government.</p><p>5. State the benefits and harms of indirect tax. (Sargodha Board 2011)</p><p>6. Discuss the merits and demerits of direct tax. (Bahawalpur Board 2011, Mirpur Azad Kashmir Board 2011)</p><p>7. Review the tax system of Pakistan. (Lahore Board 2011)</p><p>8. Present proposals to improve the tax system in Pakistan.</p><p>Question 3. More than one answer has been given for each question; of them put the mark (✓) on the correct answer.</p><p>1. The nature of income tax is this:</p><p>(a) proportional  (b) progressive ✓</p><p>(c) regressive  (d) indirect</p><p>2. The meaning of the principle of equality of imposing tax is:</p><p>(a) taking tax at one rate  (b) taking tax at a progressive rate ✓</p><p>(c) taking tax at the lowest rate</p><p>3. The burden of this tax can be transferred to another person:</p><p>(a) direct tax  (b) indirect tax ✓</p><p>(c) property tax</p><p>4. The principles of imposing tax were presented by this economist:</p><p>(a) Ricardo  (b) Adam Smith ✓</p><p>(c) J. S. Mill  (d) Marshall</p>",
