   "content": "<p>5. Excise duty is a tax of this kind:</p><p>(a) direct tax  (b) indirect tax ✓</p><p>(c) proportional tax  (d) non-proportional tax</p><p>6. The nature of income tax is:</p><p>(a) indirect  (b) direct ✓</p><p>(c) regressive  (d) equal rate</p><p>7. The best system of taxes is this:</p><p>(a) direct tax  (b) indirect tax</p><p>(c) which fulfils the principles of imposing tax ✓</p><p>8. The objective of fiscal policy:</p><p>(a) imposing more tax  (b) imposing less tax</p><p>(c) maintaining full employment (Full Employment) in the country ✓</p><p>9. Taxes imposed on goods are called:</p><p>(a) indirect tax ✓  (b) direct tax</p><p>(c) progressive tax  (d) proportional tax</p><p>10. Which is not a source of income of the central government:</p><p>(a) water rate (abiana) ✓  (b) income tax</p><p>(c) tariff  (d) wealth tax</p><p>11. All those measures which the government takes for receipts and expenses are called:</p><p>(a) agricultural policy  (b) fiscal policy ✓</p><p>(c) tax policy  (d) none of these</p><p>12. Under which principle does every person pay tax according to his capacity?</p><p>(a) principle of elasticity  (b) principle of equality ✓</p><p>(c) principle of convenience  (d) principle of diversity</p><p>13. Wealth tax is:</p><p>(a) regressive tax  (b) value-added tax</p><p>(c) proportional tax  (d) direct tax ✓</p><p>14. The burden of which tax is not transferred to poor people?</p><p>(a) excise tax  (b) sales tax</p><p>(c) income tax ✓  (d) customs duty</p><p>15. The central government collects this share of its income from taxes:</p><p>(a) 24.63%  (b) 75.32% ✓</p><p>(c) 50%  (d) 68%</p><p>16. The share of indirect taxes of the Government of Pakistan is:</p><p>(a) 68% ✓  (b) 50%</p><p>(c) 16%  (d) 18%</p>",
