     "text": "Some people earn their living by doing more than one work; e.g. in villages, besides cultivation, the cultivator also does many other works, e.g. keeping sheep and goats, keeping chickens, keeping buffaloes for selling milk. Therefore finding out the income from all these sources is difficult. In the same way a lecturer or teacher, besides his job, earns income privately by giving tuition or marking examination papers; but in the account books only his salary comes to light, the remaining income does not.",
