   "theory": "7. Of the following, one does not affect economic development:\n\n(a) natural resources  (b) language (Language) ✓\n\n(c) political situation  (d) social evils (Social Evils)\n\n8. The concept of economic development is this:\n\n(a) agricultural development  (b) industrial development\n\n(c) increase in real national income ✓  (d) increase in population\n\n9. This plan of Pakistan remained the most successful:\n\n(a) second plan  (b) third plan ✓\n\n(c) fifth plan  (d) eighth plan\n\n10. The period of Pakistan’s second five-year plan was:\n\n(a) 1950 to 1955  (b) 1955 to 1960\n\n(c) 1960 to 1965 ✓  (d) 1965 to 1970\n\n11. This is not included in the characteristics of developing countries:\n\n(a) over-population  (b) heavy quantity of capital ✓\n\n(c) dependence on agriculture  (d) export of raw material\n\n12. In Pakistan industries were taken into national custody in:\n\n(a) 1972 ✓  (b) 1974\n\n(c) 1975  (d) 1976\n\n13. The period of Pakistan’s eighth five-year plan was:\n\n(a) 1960-65  (b) 1993-98 ✓\n\n(c) 1989-94  (d) 1998-2003",
