     "text": "The State Bank of Pakistan is the central bank of our country. It was established on 1 July 1948. Its inauguration was done by Quaid-e-Azam Muhammad Ali Jinnah. On 30 June 2012 this bank completed 64 years of its life. During this time it has played a prominent role in restoring the ruined economic conditions of the country and putting it on the path of economic development. This is the most important financial institution of Pakistan, and it fulfils all those responsibilities which are entrusted to a central bank. (It is also called “Bank Daulat-e-Pakistan”.)",
