     "text": "(continued from p.198) … appointment is made for five years. It has been decided that the Central Board of Directors must hold at least six meetings in the whole year and at least one meeting in a quarter. The governor of the State Bank arranges this at the instance of the Central Board, and for this purpose forms an executive committee. On 1 July 1974 the State Bank of Pakistan was taken into national custody. Its offices are in these cities: Karachi, Lahore, Islamabad, Rawalpindi, Faisalabad, Multan, Sialkot, Gujranwala, Peshawar, Dera Ismail Khan, Hyderabad, Sukkur, Quetta, Bahawalpur, Muzaffarabad and North Nazimabad Karachi.",
