     "text": "In November 1997 the State Bank issued detailed instructions that no banking company in Pakistan can continue the business of banking until its minimum paid-up capital (Paid Up Capital) is one billion (arab) rupees, and until its reserves (Reserves) are not equal to eight per cent of its risk-weighted assets (Risk Weighted Assets).",
