   "content": "<p>(9, continued) …</p><p>A. The State Bank of Pakistan was established on 1 July 1948, and its head office is in “Karachi”.</p><p>10. What is monetary policy?</p><p>A. This is such a policy by means of which the central bank, by making the quantity of money less or more, controls prices.</p><p>11. What is an ATM?</p><p>A. This is such an automatic machine by means of which we can withdraw money from the bank whenever we want. ATM is the abbreviation of Automated Teller Machine.</p><p>12. State four important functions of the State Bank of Pakistan.</p><p>A. (i) bank of the government; (ii) economic stability; (iii) monopolist of issuing notes; (iv) guardian of the money market.</p><p>13. What is meant by e-commerce?</p><p>A. By e-commerce is meant electronic commerce. In brief it is also called e-commerce or EC (EC). This is the modern method of business on the internet.</p><p>16. State the difference between demand-pressure and cost-pushed inflation.</p><p>A. If an increase occurs in prices because of demand increasing, then it is called inflation of demand pressure; but if the increase in prices is because of the cost of production increasing, then it is called cost-push inflation.</p><p>Section II (Section II)</p><p>Question 2: Write detailed answers to the following questions:</p><p>(i) Write the functions of a commercial bank.</p><p>(ii) State the kinds of banks.</p><p>(iii) How do commercial banks create credit money? (Mirpur Azad Kashmir Board 2009)</p><p>(iv) State the general causes of inflation.</p><p>(v) State the causes of inflation in Pakistan. (Bahawalpur Board 2011)</p><p>(vi) State the remedy of the inflation prevalent in Pakistan. In this connection which measures has the government taken?</p><p>(vii) Write the effects of inflation. (Multan Board 2009)</p><p>(viii) Write a note on the National Bank of Pakistan.</p><p>(ix) State the functions of Zarai Taraqiati Bank Limited (ZTBL).</p><p>(x) State the functions of the State Bank of Pakistan. (Mirpur Azad Kashmir Board 2011)</p><p>Objective (Objective)</p><p>Question 3: More than one answer has been given for each question; of them put the mark (✓) on the correct answer.</p><p>1. The State Bank of Pakistan was established in this year:</p><p>(a) 1947  (b) 1948 ✓</p><p>(c) 1949  (d) 1950</p><p>2. The institution issuing currency notes in Pakistan:</p><p>(a) government  (b) National Bank</p><p>(c) State Bank ✓  (d) Habib Bank</p>",
