     "text": "By it is meant interest on external loans, interest on internal loans, and the amounts specified for the return of loans. Medium- and long-term external and internal debt exists on Pakistan. As far as internal and domestic debt is concerned, its payment has the status of transfer payments within the country; but as far as external debt is concerned, that is a kind of claim (Claim) on national wealth, which will be paid out of the incomes to be earned in future. The need to take loans from foreign countries arises because, on one side, the rate of saving within the country is very low, whereas for investment for economic development a very large amount is required; and on the other side, for national development it is necessary to import machines, capital goods and other goods from foreign countries. The amount of the government’s payment of interest on internal and external loans has gone on increasing continuously.",
