     "text": "Generally people keep their saved wealth as hoards, i.e. preserved in the form of cash money or ornaments. Most money does not come into use and a recession (Slump) arises. But in an Islamic society people will not keep a large quantity of money idle in the form of hoards and ornaments, because in this way, by giving zakat every year, its quantity will become less. Thus people will put their wealth in some business or other, will establish factories, will give it to someone (on the basis of partnership and mudaraba) for trade, and … (continued on p.242)",
