   "content": "<p>Model paper questions</p><p>Subjective (Subjective), Section I (Section I)</p><p>Question 1: Write short answers to the following questions:</p><p>1. What are the four important big exports of Pakistan?</p><p>A. (i) cotton thread; (ii) rice; (iii) bedwear; (iv) cotton.</p><p>2. State the benefits that accrue to Pakistan from foreign trade.</p><p>A. (i) increase in foreign exchange; (ii) improvement in economic stability; (iii) increase in employment; (iv) acquaintance with new technology.</p><p>3. What is meant by the remittances of workers?</p><p>A. When the people of Pakistan, going outside the country and earning money, send it into the country, then it is called the remittances of workers.</p><p>4. What is meant by diversification in the export heads of Pakistan?</p><p>A. The exports of Pakistan should not be of one nature, but rather should consist of different kinds; dependence cannot be made on one kind of nature.</p><p>5. Pakistan has three kinds of imports. State their names.</p><p>A. (i) capital goods; (ii) industrial raw material; (iii) consumer goods.</p><p>6. State the important imports of Pakistan.</p><p>A. (i) machinery (non-electric); (ii) petrol and products; (iii) transport equipment; (iv) chemicals; (v) food items.</p><p>7. State four reasons for disorder in the balance of payments of Pakistan.</p><p>A. (i) increase in imports; (ii) increase in the prices of imports; (iii) exports are less; (iv) decrease in workers’ remittances.</p><p>8. Which countries are included in the Economic Cooperation Organisation?</p><p>A. (i) Pakistan; (ii) Turkey; (iii) Iran.</p><p>9. Write four benefits of international trade.</p><p>A. (i) acquisition of necessary goods; (ii) surplus to need; (iii) agricultural and industrial development; (iv) means of government income.</p><p>Section II (Section II)</p><p>Question 2: Write detailed answers to the following questions:</p><p>i) State the prominent characteristics of the foreign trade of Pakistan. (Gujranwala Board 2009, Lahore Board 2011)</p><p>ii) State the importance of foreign trade in the Pakistani economy.</p>",
