   "content": "<p>Model paper questions</p><p>Subjective (Subjective), Section I (Section I)</p><p>Question 1. Write short answers to the following questions:</p><p>1. What is meant by an economic system?</p><p>A. “By an economic system is meant such an organisation in which, by using all the resources of any country, goods and services are prepared according to the necessities of life.”</p><p>2. Write the names of four important economic systems.</p><p>A. (i) capitalist system; (ii) socialist or government-authority system; (iii) Islamic economic system; (iv) non-intervention or free-business system.</p><p>3. Define the capitalist system.</p><p>A. “By the capitalist system is meant such a system of economic organisation whose important characteristic is the ‘right of private ownership’, and also that nature-made and man-made capital be used for the sake of private profit.”</p><p>4. Write four characteristics of the capitalist system.</p><p>A. (i) right of private ownership and system of inheritance; (ii) freedom to do business; (iii) discovery of new technology; (iv) promotion of saving and investment.</p><p>5. State four shortcomings of the capitalist system.</p><p>A. (i) capital is given superiority over man; (ii) improper spending on competition and advertising; (iii) concentration of wealth; (iv) economic ups and downs and instability.</p><p>6. Define the socialist or government-authority system.</p><p>A. “By it is meant such a movement whose purpose is that all nature-made and man-made capital goods (which are used for producing things on a large scale) be given, instead of to individuals, into the custody of the nation collectively for ownership and management, so that the increasing national income can be distributed equally; but in this connection no blow should fall on the economic motive of the individual or his occupational freedom and on choice and liking in connection with consuming goods.”</p><p>7. Write the names of four characteristics of the socialist system.</p><p>A. (i) productive resources in collective ownership; (ii) equal opportunities of progress; (iii) economic development; (iv) social security.</p><p>8. Write four shortcomings of the socialist system.</p><p>A. (i) ending of economic freedom; (ii) unsuitability of the government for business; (iii) the allocation of resources is not correct.</p>",
