   "content": "<p>9. Define the Islamic economic system.</p><p>A. Such an economic system which is based on Islamic principles. In the Islamic economic system there is opposition to interest, whereas there is no restriction on private property and permissible profits.</p><p>10. Write the names of four characteristics of the Islamic economic system.</p><p>A. (i) observance of Shariah limits; (ii) wide circulation of money; (iii) non-interest economy; (iv) free of exploitation.</p><p>11. Define the system of non-intervention.</p><p>A. Such an economic system in which ordinary individuals have complete business freedom, and the government does not interfere in economic matters.</p><p>Section II (Section II)</p><p>Question 2. Write detailed answers to the following questions:</p><p>i) State the characteristics of the capitalist economic system. (Mirpur Azad Kashmir Board 2010, Multan Board 2011)</p><p>ii) State the shortcomings of the capitalist system (Capitalism).</p><p>iii) Write the shortcomings of socialism.</p><p>iv) State the important characteristics of the economic system of Islam. (Multan Board 2009, Bahawalpur Board 2009, Mirpur Azad Kashmir Board 2009, Bahawalpur Board 2010)</p><p>v) In the Islamic economic system the concentration of wealth (Concentration of Wealth) has been declared forbidden. Write a note on it.</p><p>vi) Present a comparison of the Islamic economic system and the capitalist system.</p><p>vii) Make clear the economic importance of zakat.</p><p>Objective (Objective)</p><p>Question 3. More than one answer has been given for each question; of them put the mark (✓) on the correct answer.</p><p>1. Ushr is applicable on this:</p><p>(a) trade goods  (b) agricultural produce ✓</p><p>(c) industrial produce  (d) exports</p><p>2. This economic system is prevalent in Pakistan:</p><p>(a) Islamic economic system  (b) socialist system</p><p>(c) capitalist system ✓</p><p>3. In socialism who makes the basic decisions?</p><p>(a) the public  (b) the government ✓</p><p>(c) demand and supply</p><p>4. In Pakistan the distribution of wealth is such:</p><p>(a) equal  (b) unequal ✓</p><p>(c) just  (d) progressive</p><p>5. In a non-interest economy employment opportunities:</p><p>(a) increase ✓  (b) do not increase</p><p>(c) remain as they are</p>",
