   "content": "<p>Economics Inter Part-II (2018)</p><p>Paper II (objective type)</p><p>1. The formula of the quantity theory of money was presented by:</p><p>(a) Taussig  (b) Fisher</p><p>(c) Marshall  (d) Robbins</p><p>2. The principles of imposing taxes were first presented by:</p><p>(a) Adam Smith  (b) Marshall</p><p>(c) Malthus  (d) Ricardo</p><p>3. The fiscal year of Pakistan ends on:</p><p>(a) 20 March  (b) 25 April</p><p>(c) 30 May  (d) 30 June</p><p>4. The centre of the national budget is:</p><p>(a) co-operative bank  (b) savings bank</p><p>(c) foreign exchange bank  (d) commercial bank</p><p>5. In the barter system the difficulty is:</p><p>(a) abundance of goods  (b) lack of double coincidence in goods</p><p>(c) difference of language  (d) difference in professions</p><p>6. Unemployment allowance is:</p><p>(a) transfer payment  (b) net national product</p><p>(c) gross national product  (d) national income</p><p>7. Profit-and-loss sharing accounts (PLS) were introduced:</p><p>(a) in the Bhutto period  (b) in the Ayub period</p><p>(c) in the Zia-ul-Haq period  (d) in the Pervez Musharraf period</p><p>8. The theory of comparative costs was founded:</p><p>(a) on the law of demand  (b) on the law of supply</p><p>(c) on the labour theory of value  (d) on the law of substitution</p><p>9. The WTO (WTO) was established:</p><p>(a) 1980  (b) 1945</p><p>(c) 1995  (d) 1990</p><p>10. The equilibrium level of national income is:</p><p>(a) consumption = saving  (b) consumption = investment</p><p>(c) income = investment  (d) saving = investment</p>",
