   "content": "<p>Economics Inter Part-II (2019)</p><p>Paper II (objective type)</p><p>Note: four possible answers A, B, C and D have been given for each question. On the answer copy, fill the circle according to the correct answer with a marker or pen in the circles given in front of each question. In case of filling more than one circle or cutting and filling, the said answer will be considered wrong.</p><p>1. This is not included in the quantitative methods of monetary policy:</p><p>(a) open market operations  (b) bank rate policy</p><p>(c) rationing  (d) advertising</p><p>2. The government policy related to imports and exports is called:</p><p>(a) monetary policy  (b) fiscal policy</p><p>(c) trade policy  (d) price policy</p><p>3. Which is not a transfer payment?</p><p>(a) pension  (b) wage</p><p>(c) stipend  (d) alms</p><p>4. The theory of trade of absolute advantage was presented by:</p><p>(a) Adam Smith  (b) David Ricardo</p><p>(c) Pigou  (d) Marshall</p><p>5. The consumption function is related to:</p><p>(a) income and investment  (b) income and consumption</p><p>(c) income and saving  (d) income and rate of interest</p><p>6. Fiscal policy is related:</p><p>(a) to the public  (b) to the government</p><p>(c) to the central bank  (d) to the commercial bank</p><p>7. Commercial banks create:</p><p>(a) credit money  (b) token money</p><p>(c) legal tender money  (d) metallic money</p><p>8. The speculative demand for money depends:</p><p>(a) on business conditions  (b) on the rate of interest</p><p>(c) on investment  (d) on income</p><p>9. The biggest source of the government’s income is:</p><p>(a) tax  (b) fines</p><p>(c) loans  (d) deficit financing</p><p>10. That document which the buyer writes to the seller is called:</p><p>(a) cheque  (b) draft</p><p>(c) crossed cheque  (d) hundi (bill)</p>",
